{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>You.</b> He speaks to the people of Israel, and \"my servant\" is the prophet." "<b>For I am He.</b> This is the oneness stated above, for every \"is\" is not He Himself." "<b>Before me no El was formed.</b> Some say: before the standing at Mount Sinai, and \"after\" — after the standing. But there is no need; rather, it means simply: there is no El before, and likewise \"after none shall be\" — and the reason is that He is first and last. And \"formed\" is stated alongside El, for there is no El besides Him if not \"formed,\" and the foolish of heart will reckon that from the prophet's words it follows that HaShem is formed, Heaven forbid, Heaven forbid — only they do not understand the truth."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 43, :notes {2 "The word עורי (literally 'blind' or 'foolish') rendered as 'foolish of heart' following the construct with לב; the term is unusual and possibly a variant of עוורי."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:45.637015518Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}